      "source": "Wu Blockchain (Telegram)",
      "type": "telegram",
      "headline": "Tether's $4.8 Billion Stock Portfolio Spans Bitcoin Mining, Gold and Media According to Protos' analysis of U.S. regulatory filings, Tether, issuer of the world's largest stablecoin USDT, holds approximately $4.8 billion in equity exposure across 13 U.S.-listed companies spanning media, gold mining, Bitcoin mining and crypto treasury businesses. Its three largest holdings are Twenty One Capital ($1.37 billion), Rumble ($1.33 billion) and Adecoagro ($966 million), accounting for roughly 76% of the total. Several investments have performed poorly, with Twenty One Capital down about 53% since listing, while Aurelion and Antalpha have fallen roughly 91% and 90%, respectively. — link",
